    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474">

                <pb facs="0580" n="322" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg322"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/704</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The French Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Jusserand</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 6, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 8.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: My Government informs
                    me that the German Federal Council, by order dated the 25th ultimo, decreed the
                    seizure by the German authorities of all the flour and cereals then in the
                    Empire or which might reach it on and after the first of this month.</p>
                <p>In compliance with instructions received I have the honor to call to your
                    excellency’s attention one of the effects necessarily produced by that decree
                    which is to make that class of merchandise, listed as conditional contraband,
                    liable to capture whoever may be the consignee named in the bill of lading. For
                    their mere arrival in Germany places them, by virtue of the aforesaid decree, at
                    the disposal of the enemy.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jusserand</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
